{"sections":[],"kind":"symbol","primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"tokens":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"protocol"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"Destination"},{"kind":"text","text":" : "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:s8SendableP","text":"Sendable"}],"platforms":["Linux"],"languages":["swift"]}]},{"kind":"content","content":[{"text":"Overview","type":"heading","anchor":"overview","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"deliver(to:batchBufferLimit:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" gives each destination its batches in the order the events","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"were tracked, one at a time: the next batch comes once ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Destinations\/documentation\/Destinations\/Destination\/receive(_:)","type":"reference"},{"text":" returns. Batches that","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"arrive meanwhile wait in a buffer of the destination’s own, which drops its oldest batch when","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"full, so a destination that falls behind loses batches rather than holding up the others.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Destinations\/documentation\/Destinations\/Destination\/receive(_:)","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" should return as soon as the batch is somewhere it won’t be lost, and honour"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"cancellation: a delivery waits for it before it completes, and cancels it when the delivery is"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"cancelled. Until it returns, this destination’s later batches wait in its buffer. A"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"destination handles its own errors (a failed upload, say); the delivery has none to receive."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"When a tracker keeps its records in a store, returning from "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Destinations\/documentation\/Destinations\/Destination\/receive(_:)","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" is what tells the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"store a batch arrived: once every destination has returned for it, uncancelled, the store"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"forgets those records. A destination that buffers or retries should return only once the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"batch is somewhere it won’t be lost; a record whose "},{"code":"EventRecord.isRedelivered","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" is set may"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"have reached it in an earlier run."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"What a destination receives is narrowed by modifiers rather than by code of its own:"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Destinations\/documentation\/Destinations\/Destination\/accepting(_:)"},{"type":"text","text":" for the consent categories it serves, "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Destinations\/documentation\/Destinations\/Destination\/redactingSensitiveValues()"},{"type":"text","text":" and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Destinations\/documentation\/Destinations\/Destination\/droppingCallSite()"},{"type":"text","text":". A destination given none receives every record as tracked."}]}]}],"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/Destinations\/documentation\/Destinations\/Destination"},"topicSections":[{"anchor":"Instance-Methods","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Destinations\/documentation\/Destinations\/Destination\/accepting(_:)","doc:\/\/Destinations\/documentation\/Destinations\/Destination\/droppingCallSite()","doc:\/\/Destinations\/documentation\/Destinations\/Destination\/receive(_:)","